{'symbol': 'RSG', 'date': '2021-12-01 09:04:00', 'title': 'NEW REPUBLIC SERVICES FACILITY HELPING TURN FOOD WASTE INTO RENEWABLE ENERGY', 'text': "PHOENIX, DEC. 1, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0REPUBLIC SERVICES, INC. (NYSE: RSG) TODAY ANNOUNCED THE OPENING OF THE SACRAMENTO AREA'S FIRST ORGANICS PRE-PROCESSING FACILITY, WHICH WILL HELP LOCAL COMMUNITIES DIVERT FOOD WASTE FROM LANDFILLS AND TURN IT INTO RENEWABLE ENERGY. A NEW CALIFORNIA STATE LAW, SB 1383, AIMED AT COMBATING CLIMATE CHANGE TAKES EFFECT JAN. 1, 2022, AND WILL REQUIRE THE MAJORITY OF CALIFORNIA HOMES AND BUSINESS TO RECYCLE FOOD AND YARD WASTE AT FACILITIES SUCH AS THIS ONE."}